64. PERFORMANCE MEASURES

3H must be measurable.

Primary measures:

prediction calibration

prediction improvement

failure recurrence

diagnosis accuracy

diagnosis latency

adaptation success rate

adaptation rejection rate

rollback rate

regression rate

learning-candidate validation rate

false-learning rate

drift-detection quality

health-detection quality

recovery time

recovery success rate

resource reliability estimation accuracy

self-model accuracy

improvement persistence

learning cost

compute consumed by learning

human intervention required

adaptation churn rate

average adaptation observation window

repeated-change frequency



---

65. EXPLICIT NON-ASSUMPTIONS

3H does not assume:

every outcome contains a lesson

every failure requires adaptation

every successful result proves correctness

every failure proves strategy weakness

latest data is most important

more learning automatically means more intelligence

continual learning automatically improves performance

more model updates = better model

more adaptations = better CNS

every drift requires model replacement

every challenger should replace champion

higher benchmark score = better ecosystem

one metric defines improvement

one failure identifies one cause

correlation = causation

human correction = universal truth

simulation = reality

paper performance = live performance

learning can bypass financial controls

learning can bypass governance

self-improvement means unrestricted self-modification

recovery means simply restarting

health means availability

health score means safety

every learning candidate requires full 3F verification

every learning candidate can bypass 3F when research-grade verification is required

complexity = intelligence

constant change = improvement



