67. FINAL CHECKER ATTACK — V1.1

I attacked the corrected architecture again.

Can one outcome rewrite CNS?

No.

Evidence assessment and learning-candidate validation stand between outcome and adaptation.

Can 3H become a second 3F?

No.

The operational-learning path and research-verification path are explicitly separated.

Can a research-grade claim bypass 3F?

No.

The validation path explicitly routes such claims to 3F.

Can 3H promote a financial-risk change by itself?

No.

The adaptation authority matrix prevents that.

Can a system-wide change receive lightweight testing?

No.

Impact classification determines validation depth.

Can CNS endlessly oscillate between adaptations?

Controlled against.

Observation windows, cooldowns, concurrent-change limits, lineage and churn detection are explicit.

Can “health = 82” accidentally mean “safe”?

No.

Health profile is authoritative; summary score is only a projection. Critical flags override it.

Can 3H become the universal recovery engine?

No.

3H learns and recommends; the responsible subsystem executes recovery.

Can one repeated observation become a universal lesson?

No.

Evidence strength explicitly tracks independence, replication, OOS evidence, regime coverage and contradiction.

Can a challenger win because of one attractive metric?

No.

Multi-metric champion/challenger evaluation is required.

Can adaptation bypass rollback?

No.

Accepted changes carry rollback references and deployment state.

Can the learning system itself become unhealthy?

Yes — and now it can detect that.

Learning-system failure is an explicit acceptance test and health concern.

Can learning bypass 3G?

No.

Financial authority remains in 3G.

Can learning bypass 3I?

No.

Security/governance authority remains in 3I.

Can 3H authorize resumption after recovery?

No.

The responsible subsystem and applicable governance/safety boundaries retain resume authority. 3H evaluates the learning and health implications.

Are learning validation and adaptation validation the same thing?

No.

Learning validation establishes whether the lesson is sufficiently supported.

Adaptation validation establishes whether the proposed change is safe, effective, and acceptable for deployment.

Did the seven corrections require another log?

No.

Everything belongs naturally inside 3H.


